== option 3: the unique key gains a generation (0 for the live row, a fresh value for each tombstone)
  ok      a live row at /d/a.txt
  ok      tombstone it, generation = its own row id
  ok      a second, live row at /d/a.txt
  ok      tombstone the second too
  ok      a third, live row at /d/a.txt
  REFUSED a fourth, live row at /d/a.txt (must be refused): UNIQUE constraint failed: e.parent_id, e.name, e.generation
  REFUSED restore the first while the third is live (must be refused): UNIQUE constraint failed: e.parent_id, e.name, e.generation
